From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:48:04 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] platform-fds

The Famicom Disk System gets one shelf, Games/FDS, on fceumm alone.
Platform::Fds is appended to SHELVES; Core::EVERY and upstream's ALL
lists stay as they are. Disks are .fds files, titled by their stem.
Every policy method answers the Disk System explicitly and the same as
the NES: L1 and R1 stay slot's (the disk control drives the core's own
L and R, patch fds-disk), L2 and R2 stay slot's rewind and fast-forward,
no core picker (Nestopia never runs a disk), the NES overscan crop,
rewind on. The 256x240 picture uses fceumm's 360x240 canvas, Crop by
default. Its shader is stored in Config/fds_shader.txt and offers the
retro list. Saves/FDS, States/FDS and Labels/FDS are made at boot. The
release year order puts it after the Master System (21 February 1986).
The shelf shows the Famicom cart until the disk lands.
